# Day 58

**39km / 9.5 hours**

*Bulls to Palmerston North*

Lots of road walking. Out of Bulls after crossing the bridge there was a state highway crossing and then it was a long side road for a while before getting into Feilding, a charming little town that spells their name funny. Stopped a bit for lunch and then continued onwards for more road. This time it was a long straight sidewalk before a little farm walking into Bunnythorpe, which is a small village, then finally back to the road into Palmerston North.

![The view of the river from the bridge crossing near the start of the day](./river.avif)

Palmerston North(or Palmy) is weird because it's more like a big town than a city. Walking past the airport then the endless suburbs with massive roads and tricky crossings was not appealing though. Did get through to the city centre in the end.

![Palmy in all its glory(?)](./palmy.avif)